              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "To log into your Microsoft OneDrive account, you can use any of the options below depending on how you want to access your files:\n\n### 1. Web Browser (Direct Link)\nYou can access OneDrive from any device using a web browser:\n*   **Direct Login Link:** Go directly to the **[OneDrive Sign-in Page](https://onedrive.live.com)**.\n*   **Alternative Option:** You can also go to **[Microsoft 365](https://www.microsoft365.com)**, sign in, and click on the **OneDrive icon** (the blue cloud) from the App Launcher in the top-left corner.\n*   **Steps:** \n    1. Enter your Microsoft account email address, phone number, or Skype name.\n    2. Click **Next**.\n    3. Enter your password and click **Sign in**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Windows 10 / 11 Desktop App\nOneDrive is already built into Windows 10 and 11:\n1. Click the **Start menu** (or press the Windows key).\n2. Type **OneDrive** and select the OneDrive app from the search results.\n3. If it is your first time opening it, a setup window will prompt you to enter your email address.\n4. Enter your email and password, then follow the on-screen instructions to select which folders you want to sync.\n* *(If you are on a Mac, you can download the OneDrive app from the Mac App Store.)*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Mobile App (Android / iPhone)\nIf you are trying to access your files on your phone or tablet:\n1. Download the official **Microsoft OneDrive** app from the App Store (iOS) or Google Play Store (Android).\n2. Open the app and tap **Sign in**.\n3. Enter your Microsoft account credentials (email and password) to access your cloud storage.\n\n***\n\n**Need Help?**\n* **Forgot your password?** If you cannot log in, click the **\"Forgot password?\"** or **\"Can't access your account?\"** link on the login page to recover it.\n* **Work or School Accounts:** If you are using a professional account, use your school or company email address. It will automatically redirect you to your organization's custom login portal.",
